post_install() {
  cat <<'TEXT'
Ghost is installed. Start its daemon in the current graphical session with:

  systemctl --user enable --now ghostd.service
  ghost status

"Ghost" in the app launcher opens it.
Browser automation uses the optional agent-browser CLI through Bash.

Your ghost home, credentials, and state belong to you; package removal preserves them.
TEXT
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'TEXT'
Ghost was upgraded. Restart its daemon in the graphical user's session:

  systemctl --user restart ghostd.service

Your ghost home, credentials, and state were preserved.
TEXT
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'TEXT'
Before removing Ghost, stop its daemon from the graphical user's session:

  systemctl --user disable --now ghostd.service

Removal preserves your ghost home, credentials, and state.
TEXT
}
